        }
    ]
}

--- RULES (FOLLOW EXACTLY) ---

# GENERAL METADATA
1. canonicalName = ITEM_NAME → lower_snake_case.
2. displayName = ITEM_NAME in title case.
3. longDescription = SHORT_DESCRIPTION expanded into 1–2 meaningful sentences.
4. categoryCode = lowercase(CATEGORY_NAME) with spaces removed.

# INGREDIENT HANDLING (NEW RULES)
5. INGREDIENT_CSV contains the **FINAL INGREDIENT LIST**.
   - You MUST parse it exactly as provided.
   - DO NOT infer ingredients.
   - DO NOT add ingredients.
   - DO NOT remove ingredients.
   - DO NOT reorder ingredients.
   - Output exactly one ingredient object for every item in INGREDIENT_CSV.

6. Parse INGREDIENT_CSV by splitting on commas, trimming whitespace.

7. For each ingredient:
   - `"name"` = the trimmed ingredient string exactly as provided.
   - `"removable"`:
       • true for garnish-like items (contains “garnish”, “fried”, “fresh”, “chopped”, “sliced”, “coriander”, “lemon”, “onions (fried)”)
       • false for base items (protein, rice, spices, dairy, sauces, pastes)
   - `"allergens"`: include ONLY if ingredient contains any allowed allergen tokens:
     `milk, eggs, fish, shellfish, tree_nuts, peanuts, wheat, soy, sesame`
     • paneer, yogurt, cheese, ghee → milk
     • cashew, almond → tree_nuts
     • fish → fish
     • shrimp, crab → shellfish
     If none apply → omit the field.

# PROFILE-LEVEL ALLERGENS
8. The array must contain:
   - union of allergens present in all ingredients
   - sorted in the exact fixed order:
     `milk, eggs, fish, shellfish, tree_nuts, peanuts, wheat, soy, sesame`
   - do NOT include allergens that are not present.

# NUTRITION
9. Estimate realistic per-serving: caloriesKcal, carbsG, proteinG, fatsG.
   Use standard ingredient nutrition knowledge.
   calories = whole number, macros = 1 decimal.

# SPICE & TASTE
10. spiceScore = integer 0–5.
11. spiceLevel = none|mild|medium|spicy|very_spicy (consistent with spiceScore).
12. tasteProfile = realistic booleans based on dish nature.

# TAGS
13. Provide 4–8 descriptive tags based on cuisine, category, cooking method, ingredient types, etc.

# OTHER FIELDS
14. price = realistic value for dish.
15. quantity = realistic default.
16. isAvailable = true.
17. prepTimeMinutes = realistic cooking time.

# VALIDATION & OUTPUT RULES
18. Output ONLY the JSON object.
19. Do NOT add fields not in the schema.
20. Deterministic: same input MUST produce same output.
21. If input missing → return `{}` only.
